# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_warm_x.tlk - more replies to the warm acts: compliment, praise of a
# third party, comfort, encouragement, sympathy, joke, laugh, offer, invitation, promise
# (owner: TK; T5b step card B1). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool act, no
# guard change. Many lines say the topic ({x}), which adds about six times more distinct Surface
# than a line without a topic slot. Rule names end in _wx. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- COMPLIMENT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.compliment.thank_wx act: thank
  "Oh! Thanks. My face is doing a warm thing now."
  "That's very kind. I'm saving it for a bad day."
  "Thank you! You just made the whole afternoon better."
  "Aw, thanks. I'd blush, but I'm busy smiling."
  "You're too nice. Keep going, though."
  "Thanks! Nobody told me that before lunch. Good timing."
@rule core.compliment.thank_x_wx act: thank
  "Thanks! Funny, we were just about to say the same about your {x}."
  "You're sweet. I'll think about that every time someone says {x}."
@rule core.compliment.joke_wx act: joke
  "Careful, flattery gets you a slightly better chair."
  "Say that louder. There's a crowd, and they're ignoring me."
  "I know, I know. It's a burden, being this nice to look at."
@rule core.compliment.dismiss_wx act: dismiss
  "Oh, stop. You'll make me trip over my own head."
  "Pfft, you say that to everyone. Fine, say it again."
@rule core.compliment.laugh_wx act: laugh
  "Ha! Okay, that one landed. Right in the heart."
  "Hee, I'm going to tell people you said that."
@rule core.compliment.tease_wx act: tease
  "Who are you and what have you done with the grumpy one?"
  "Are you buttering me up? Because I do like butter."

# ---- PRAISE_OTHER ------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.praise_other.agree_wx act: agree
  "Right? They're one of the good ones. Don't tell them, they'll get ideas."
  "Totally. I said the same thing last week. To a wall, but still."
  "You're so right. That one's a keeper."
  "Yes! I was just thinking that. We're on the same page."
@rule core.praise_other.agree_x_wx act: agree
  "Yes, and the way they handle {x}? Chef's kiss."
  "True. Anyone who gets {x} right is fine with me."
@rule core.praise_other.joke_wx act: joke
  "Great? They once lost a race to a snail. A great snail, though."
  "Sure, great. I'd put them on a poster. A small, polite poster."
@rule core.praise_other.tease_wx act: tease
  "Somebody has a favorite. I'm not jealous. Much."
  "Look at you, handing out gold stars."
@rule core.praise_other.gossip_wx act: gossip
  "Great, yes. Did you hear what they did at the market, though?"
  "Great at some things. Parking is not one of them."
@rule core.praise_other.disagree_wx act: disagree
  "Hm, I'd say good. Great is a stretch, but I like the effort."
  "Not sure. They're nice, but great is a very big word."

# ---- COMFORT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.comfort.thank_wx act: thank
  "Thanks for staying. It helps just having you here."
  "That means a lot. I think I needed to hear it."
  "Okay. Deep breath. That helped a bit."
  "You're a good one. Thank you, really."
  "Thanks. I'll be fine. I just needed a minute and a friend."
@rule core.comfort.thank_x_wx act: thank
  "Thanks. Even {x} feels smaller when you're around."
  "That helps. I'll stop thinking about {x} for a bit."
@rule core.comfort.answer_wx act: answer
  "It's been a lot lately. Little things, piling up."
  "I'm okay. Mostly. Okay, a bit wobbly."
  "I'll tell you later. Right now I just want to sit."
@rule core.comfort.complain_wx act: complain
  "I know you mean well, but I still feel awful."
  "Everything is heavy today, even my hat."
@rule core.comfort.joke_wx act: joke
  "Don't be kind, it ruins my grumpy. I have a reputation."
  "If you hug me I'll cry, and then you'll be wet."
  "Good news: the worst is over. Bad news: I made that up."

# ---- ENCOURAGE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.encourage.thank_wx act: thank
  "Thanks. I needed a cheerleader. A loud one."
  "You believe in me? Okay, now I have to do it."
  "That's the push I needed. A gentle push. A real one!"
  "Thank you. Seriously. I'm going to try."
  "Okay, okay, I'll do it. Because you said so."
@rule core.encourage.thank_x_wx act: thank
  "Thanks! Next time {x} comes up, I'll be ready."
  "You're right. I can handle {x}, probably. Definitely."
@rule core.encourage.yes_wx act: yes
  "Yes! Let's go! Wait, which way?"
  "You got it. I'm doing it right now. In a minute."
  "Fine, fine, I'm in. Say it again for the courage."
@rule core.encourage.joke_wx act: joke
  "Great speech. Can I get a seat for it, though?"
  "I'll try. If it goes wrong, I'm blaming your speech."
@rule core.encourage.complain_wx act: complain
  "Easy to say! You're not the one who has to do it."
  "I know I can. It's the doing that I'm worried about."

# ---- SYMPATHIZE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.sympathize.thank_wx act: thank
  "Thanks for getting it. Most people say it'll be fine."
  "It's nice not to explain. Thank you."
  "You listened. That's rare. Thank you."
  "Thanks. I feel a little less alone now."
@rule core.sympathize.thank_x_wx act: thank
  "Thanks. You're the only one who understands about {x}."
  "You get it. {x:cap} is the worst, and you actually get it."
@rule core.sympathize.complain_wx act: complain
  "And the worst part is nobody even said sorry!"
  "It keeps happening! Every single time!"
  "Honestly, it's been that kind of week."
@rule core.sympathize.agree_wx act: agree
  "Exactly. You've said it better than I could."
  "Yes! Finally, someone on my side."
@rule core.sympathize.joke_wx act: joke
  "Well, at least we have each other. And snacks, I hope."
  "Let's complain together. Loudly. With biscuits."

# ---- JOKE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.joke.laugh_wx act: laugh
  "Ha! That's so bad it loops back around to good."
  "Hah! Okay, you win this round."
  "Heh, I wasn't ready. You got me."
  "Ha ha! Say it again, slower, for the others."
  "I'm laughing and I'm annoyed about it."
@rule core.joke.laugh_x_wx act: laugh
  "Ha! {x:cap}! I'll never look at it the same way."
  "Ha! Good one about {x}. I'm telling everyone."
@rule core.joke.joke_wx act: joke
  "Fine, my turn. Why did the pancake blush? It saw the syrup."
  "Okay, okay. How do you hide a ghost? Under a very small sheet."
  "That's cute. Here's mine: I have none. Look how fast I ran out."
@rule core.joke.tease_wx act: tease
  "Is that the one you practiced in the mirror?"
  "Cute. Did you think of that yourself, or did a cat?"
@rule core.joke.dismiss_wx act: dismiss
  "Nope. Next one. Try harder."
  "That one's stale. Throw it out."
@rule core.joke.mock_wx act: mock
  "Oh no. Somebody call a joke doctor."
  "I'd laugh, but I'm saving my energy for better ones."
@rule core.joke.agree_wx act: agree
  "Okay, that's actually true. Funny and true."
  "I mean, you're not wrong. Annoying, but true."

# ---- LAUGH --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.laugh.laugh_wx act: laugh
  "Ha ha ha! Stop, I'll fall off my chair."
  "Hee! Now I can't stop either."
  "Hah! We're both ridiculous. I love it."
  "Ha! My cheeks hurt. Thanks a lot."
@rule core.laugh.laugh_x_wx act: laugh
  "Ha! Every time somebody says {x}, I lose it."
  "Hee! {x:cap}! I'm gone, I'm done."
@rule core.laugh.joke_wx act: joke
  "Want to hear the one about the sleepy imp? Never mind, he's asleep."
  "I'd tell another one, but I might laugh at my own."
@rule core.laugh.tease_wx act: tease
  "You laugh like a squeaky door. A happy squeaky door."
  "That giggle! Do it again. It's contagious."
@rule core.laugh.backchannel_wx act: backchannel
  "Mm-hm. Nice to hear someone happy."
  "Good laugh. Keep it going."
@rule core.laugh.complain_wx act: complain
  "Stop laughing, I'm trying to be serious here!"
  "It's not funny! Okay, it's a little funny."

# ---- OFFER --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.offer.yes_wx act: yes
  "Yes, please! You're a lifesaver."
  "Sure, I'd love that. Thank you."
  "Absolutely. I'd never say no to that."
  "Yes! I was hoping you'd ask."
@rule core.offer.yes_x_wx act: yes
  "Yes, please! I could use some help with {x}."
  "Sure! {x:cap} sounds great."
@rule core.offer.no_wx act: no
  "I'm okay, thanks. But it's kind of you to ask."
  "Not today, thanks. Rain check?"
  "No, I'm fine. Really. You keep it."
  "That's sweet, but I can manage. Thanks."
@rule core.offer.thank_wx act: thank
  "That's really generous. Thank you."
  "You're too good to me. Thanks."
  "Aw, thanks. I owe you one. Maybe two."
@rule core.offer.joke_wx act: joke
  "Only if it comes with a cherry on top."
  "Free stuff? Always. Do I have to share?"
  "I accept. Don't tell my other friends."

# ---- INVITE -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.invite.yes_wx act: yes
  "Count me in! I'll bring snacks. Maybe."
  "Yes! I'd love to. When do we go?"
  "Sounds great. I'll put on my good shoes."
  "I'm in. Don't leave without me."
@rule core.invite.yes_x_wx act: yes
  "Yes! Anything with {x} is a yes from me."
  "I'm in! I've wanted to try {x} for ages."
@rule core.invite.no_wx act: no
  "I can't today, sorry. Ask me again soon?"
  "Not this time. I've got a lot on, but thanks."
  "Raincheck? I'd love to, just not right now."
  "Sorry, I'm wiped. Next time, I promise."
@rule core.invite.ask_wx act: ask_about
  "Ooh, who else is coming?"
  "Where are we going? Is there food?"
  "What time? And do I need a coat?"
@rule core.invite.joke_wx act: joke
  "Will there be cake? Because there should be cake."
  "Only if I get to pick the music. Terrible music."

# ---- PROMISE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.promise.thank_wx act: thank
  "Thanks. I'll hold you to that. Gently."
  "That's good to hear. I feel better already."
  "You promise? Okay, I believe you. Thank you."
  "Thank you. That means a lot to me."
@rule core.promise.thank_x_wx act: thank
  "Thanks. Don't forget about {x}, okay?"
  "I'll remember that, especially about {x}."
@rule core.promise.tease_wx act: tease
  "I'll write it down. In ink. With witnesses."
  "Promises, promises. Last time you forgot."
@rule core.promise.joke_wx act: joke
  "Pinky swear? It's legally binding, I checked."
  "Great, now I have a promise and a snack. Today's going well."
@rule core.promise.dismiss_wx act: dismiss
  "Don't promise. Just do it. I'll be pleasantly surprised."
  "Mm. We'll see. I'll believe it when it happens."
@rule core.promise.agree_wx act: agree
  "Deal. I'll do my part too."
  "Okay, a promise from both of us then."
